      <div type="clause" n="2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ger">Ger</ref> 2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="453" ed="#liebermann"/>[2] Hede se ðe scire healde, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he friðige ⁊ forðige ælce be ðam ðe hit selest sy; ⁊ be ðam he eac mot, ðe hine weder wisað.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#gobbitt" n="22.2" corresp="#wit-b">Hede se ðe scire healde þæt he friðige 7 forðige ælce be ðam ðe hit se lest sy . 7 be ðam he eac mot ðe hine weder wisað .</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="332" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Hede se ðe scire healde þæt he friðige and forðige ælce be ðam ðe hit selest sy, and be ðam he eac mot ðe hine weder wisað.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="453" ed="#liebermann"/>Beobachte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#Ger_2.lnote.de1.a"/> wer das Amt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="f" target="#Ger_2.lnote.de1.f"/> innehat, dass er schütze und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="g" target="#Ger_2.lnote.de1.g"/> fördere jede gemäss dem, wie es am besten sei; und auch gemäss dem muss er [es<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="h" target="#Ger_2.lnote.de.h"/>], wie ihn das Wetter anweist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Let him who holds the office [of estate management] see to it that he protects and furthers each [task] in the way that is best; and also he must [do it] according to what the weather directs him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#gobbitt" corresp="#wit-b">The one who would oversee a shire must take heed that he promotes and furthers each [duty] as it should be attended to, and for that he must be guided by the weather.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="333" ed="#rabin-doml"/>The person who wishes to oversee a shire must take care to observe and carry out each of these as is most needed, and also to be guided by the weather.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="387"><ref target="clause:Rect_4-3-to-4-3c">Rect 4.3c</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">‘friðige ⁊ forðige’ is an alliterating pair. Liebermann compares Rect 4.6.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">shire: A term for a county or other administrative subunits of land.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ger_2.lnote.de1.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">453</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Rect. 2<hi rend="italic">ᵇ</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> Rect. 2<hi rend="italic">ᵇ</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ger_2.lnote.de1.f" n="f" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">453</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">der Gutsverwaltung</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">of the estate administration</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ger_2.lnote.de1.g" n="g" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">453</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Alliterationspaar</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">alliterative pair</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ger_2.lnote.de.h" n="h" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">252</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘soll handeln’ Sk-Wi</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘shall act’ Sk-Wi</seg></note>
      </div>
